WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.334
-Welcome to the show.
You look sharp.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.534
You look great, bud.
-Thanks, bud.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.300
I have a great stylist.
Warren Alfie Baker.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.367
Shout-out to Warren.
-Yeah, nice job.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.501
-Yeah.
-I want to go through a couple

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:10.834
things I think that we have
in common.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.434
-Yeah.
-First of all, I heard that

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:14.534
we both drive trucks.
-Yeah. You have a truck?

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.334
I have a pickup truck,
a Ford F-150.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:18.701
-Ford F-150.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.300
I have a Raptor.
Do you have a Raptor?

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.934
-No. I love the Raptor.
-Raptors are pretty cool, man.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.934
They're like a super truck.

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:26.901
I didn't need it.
I bought it when I was in L.A.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:29.567
'cause I had a business
and we sold merch,

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:31.467
and I had to move merch around.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:34.267
But like a regular F-150,
I was like, I could get that,

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.934
or I could spend twice as much
and have a truck that was ready

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:38.601
for the zombie apocalypse
and I was like

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:41.267
I'm going to go with that.
-They're cool-looking.

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.033
You go, oh, wow. No, I got mine.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:46.100
I got a Ford F-150. I'm getting
the new one, the electric.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.300
-Oh! Oh, the electric one?
The Lightning?

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.868
I want to get that one.
-I went to the factory

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.000
and watched them build it
and everything in Detroit.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.334
-Stop.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.434
-Can you tell them I'd like one?

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:55.868
Can I get the Jimmy --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:57.801
-Get the Jimmy Fallon
skip the line, yeah.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.300
-Thank you.
-I got mine to a --

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.734
'Cause every Halloween, I get
a couple of pumpkins

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.033
and I need to put
them in something.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:05.167
[ Laughter ]
So, I got a truck.

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.467
I put a couple pumpkins
in the back.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:07.901
-You got to go on
those pumpkin runs, man.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.534
-Pumpkin run, man.
It happens once a year,

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.767
but you've got to make sure.
-Pumpkin runs for the people.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:12.434
Not gonna put them in the back
of a car.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:13.767
They need to be in the back
of a truck.

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.100
I love my truck.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.934
-But you haul things too?
Like, real stuff?

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.434
-I mean, every once --
I'm really honestly,

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:20.133
like, I love it.
It's great.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.801
I live on a ranch.
I moved up to Austin,

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.667
and I have a bunch of
land up there,

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.634
so it's very helpful for that.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:28.100
But moving out, I hauled, like,
a U-Haul out there.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.400
And then I went
and got an Airstream.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.734
My first house out
there was an Airstream.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.701
-What? Now, that's next level.
-Yeah.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:35.133
-I have the attachment.
-Stop it!

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.968
-I can hook things to my truck.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:39.200
-Stop it!
-But I have not --

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.334
That's as far as I've taken it.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.100
-Well, listen. I'm not --
-"I could something with this."

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.467
-I'm not very good
at towing things.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.701
I'm surprised I didn't get
pulled over multiple times.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:49.467
But I was able to pull my
Airstream to my property.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.601
And I lived in my little silver
potato for a while.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:52.968
It was great.
-Wow!

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:54.868
What's it like living in
an Airstream?

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.901
-Honestly, I love it
'cause I love

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.234
little tiny homes and things.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.100
I'm just not a very tiny person.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.100
-You're big.
How tall are you?

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.634
-6'4", 6'5"-ish.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:05.033
-Depending on if I'm slouching.
-Whoo!

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.300
-I like the "whoo."
-Yeah.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.267
-Was that for 6'4" or for 6'5"?

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.267
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:12.634
-Boo, 6'4."

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.133
6'5"? Ow!

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.300
-I have these, like --
I loved living in it.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.834
Honestly, I could have done
a lot longer.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:22.601
But the shower in it -- my -- I
have abnormally wide shoulders.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.901
And so, I would be facing
the shower.

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:26.901
And I'd be, like, washing
the front of me.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:29.267
But you have to stay really
tidy, and then I would just try

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:32.100
to turn around and my shoulders
would pop the door open.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.767
And then all the shower water
would be pouring out.

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:35.968
I'm like, "This is not --"
-It doesn't work for you.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:37.834
-"This is not tenable.
I can't do this anymore."

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:40.334
-Another one of the things I
heard that we have in common is

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:42.601
we both did impressions
when we were kids.

00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:44.334
-Oh, yeah.
-You did?

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:45.701
-Well, yeah.
I mean, don't we all?

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.033
I guess. I don't know.
-I don't know.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.367
I don't think everyone does.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.434
-Well, I guess. I don't know.

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:53.133
I grew up watching
so many cartoons.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:55.234
I mean, I think I learned how to
act from Bugs Bunny, honestly.

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:57.601
Like, you know, I mean, just all
the voices and all the things,

00:02:57.601 --> 00:02:59.334
all the Saturday morning
cartoons and all that.

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:01.267
-You did all those?
-Yeah, I mean, you know.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.868
But then everybody --
Well, I guess not everybody,

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:06.300
but some people,
yuk-yuks like us,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.567
we like to do, you know,
impressions like Walken,

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:10.334
but everybody's got a Walken.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.734
-Christopher Walken is always
good to have.

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.267
-Yeah, Christopher Walken,
[as Walken] you know.

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:17.634
[ Normal voice ]
But what I always thought --

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:19.534
I wonder if Walken
has a Schwarzenegger

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:21.300
and I wonder if Schwarzenegger
has a Walken.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.434
You know what I mean?

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:23.667
-So, like, if they do
impressions?

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:25.300
-[ as Walken ]
Get to the chopper, come on.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.400
[ Normal voice ]
You know, like that.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:30.067
Like, come on.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.734
-"Come on, get in --
get to the chopper."

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:32.868
-"Come with me."

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.167
-"You're telling me
get to the chopper?"

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.367
-[ as Walken ] Come with me if
you want to live, Jimmy.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.834
You know.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.968
Or, like Schwarzenegger, like --
you know, it's always, like,

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.801
those famous, like, Walken
monologues, you know, so...

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:45.334
[ as Schwarzenegger ]
It's like, "I had this watch,

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:46.334
it was your father's watch.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:48.100
I hid it in my ass
for five years."

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:53.300
-I've never seen Schwarzenegger
do Christopher Walken.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.667
-[ Normal voice ] I know. I'm
like, "They got to have one."

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.968
-That's fantastic. I love that.

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:58.267
Can we talk about
"Shazam! Fury of the Gods"?

00:03:58.267 --> 00:03:59.334
-Yes, I would love to.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.334
-Congrats. Congrats on this.

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:03.267
-I would love to.
-Giant, giant, giant movie.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.334
-Yeah.
-Big movie.

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:05.267
You got to be psyched about
this.

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:06.934
The first one crushed.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:09.734
I read somewhere that you
auditioned for Shazam

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.033
or for a different role.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.968
-Yeah, so, the long
and the short of it --

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:14.000
I'll try to keep it short --
but basically --

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.133
-No, dude. Make it long.
We won't care.

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.334
-Let me take all the time.
-We love you.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:18.734
-Thank you, man.
I appreciate that.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:21.834
So, look, a couple months before
I got the job, I was offered

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:23.467
an audition for
the role of Shazam,

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.534
but I knew enough about
the character of

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:28.200
Shazam Captain Marvel that he
had, like, an evil twin named

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.968
Black Adam, and Black Adam was
being played by The Rock.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:32.868
And I was like, "Well, wait.
So they're supposed to be twins?

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:35.267
Like, there's no way
I'm getting this job."

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:36.701
-"Just so you know, I'm not
getting this one."

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:38.567
-Yeah, totally.
And also, unbeknownst to me,

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.868
I was in kind of a dark place
in my life at that point.

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:43.234
And then fast-forward about
a month and a half later,

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:45.667
and I'm in this super-intensive,
life-saving therapy

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:47.167
and I learned how to love
myself, really,

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:48.734
for the first time in my life,
and I have this whole

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.067
breakthrough, and then --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:52.734
Thank you. Thank you.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:55.267
By the way, go love yourself.

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.300
If you learn nothing else today,
go love yourself,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.868
go love yourself,
go love yourself. Okay?

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:00.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.300
So, even though I tell my agents
I was like,

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.701
"Hey, I'm going to be off grid
for a little while."

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:05.968
They're like, "Yeah, yeah.
Totally."

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:09.000
Two and a half weeks in,
they're like, "So, listen."

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.200
There's an audition, it's
for a whole other role.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.067
It's a supporting role.
If you want to do it, cool.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.200
If not, that's fine too.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.200
We understand you're doing
some healing."

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.033
I was like, "Cool."

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:16.901
I just had this breakthrough.

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:18.267
I'm like, "I'll go, whatever.

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:19.501
I feel good about myself.
I'll go and do --"

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.434
I did one take. I sent it in.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:23.934
And then in the course of,
basically one week, I ended up

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:27.033
going from auditioning for this
whole other role to them saying,

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:28.601
"Hey, we think
you're our Shazam."

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:29.868
They flew me to L.A.

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.801
I had done all my therapy
that I needed to do.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:33.234
I go to L.A. I audition.

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:34.734
And within one week,
I was Shazam.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.033
And it was all --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:37.734
Yeah, it was super crazy, man.

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:39.534
-Good for you, bud.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:41.901
-That is so good.
What a great story.

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:43.767
-Yeah, I just think it's
indicative of, you guys,

00:05:43.767 --> 00:05:46.334
when we do the real work, when
we do the work to heal ourselves

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:47.934
and help other people heal
themselves,

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:49.567
and that's where all
the good stuff comes from.

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:52.033
You know? And that's where that
blessing landed in my life.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:54.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I'm so happy.

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:57.400
What going on in this "Shazam"?
What can we tell people?

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.400
-So much. So, in the first
movie, Billy Batson,

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.901
the kid that I am the super
version of, he was 14.

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:05.834
Now he's 17, almost 18, so he's
about to age out of

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:08.167
the foster-care system, so he's
kind of freaking out about that

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.601
'cause he doesn't want to lose
this family he just found.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:14.133
And then he's feeling a little
imposter syndrome like we all do

00:06:14.133 --> 00:06:16.501
'cause he's supposed to be
the very competent leader of

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:19.601
his super family but he's really
blowing it a lot of the time.

00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:21.601
And then there's these three
goddesses played by

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:23.968
Dame Helen Mirren, Lucy Liu,
and Rachel Zegler,

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:25.133
who come to --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:26.634
-They are honestly --
-They are so great.

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:30.234
So great. And they come to kill
me and my family.

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:32.200
So, there's a lot going on.
-Yeah.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:35.234
A lot of action, a lot of comedy
as well, by the way.

00:06:35.234 --> 00:06:37.400
-Yeah, lots of fun.
-You do a really great job.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.634
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Zachary Levi

00:06:39.634 --> 00:06:42.534
in "Shazam! Fury of the Gods."
Take a look at this.

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:44.701
-Okay, look. I might not have as
much experience as you

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:47.033
'cause I'm not, like, super old
like you.

00:06:47.033 --> 00:06:50.067
But I think I have a few
experiences that you don't have

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:53.167
'cause I've seen all the "Fast &amp;
the Furious" movies, lady.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:54.934
And let me tell you something.

00:06:54.934 --> 00:06:57.968
It's all about family!

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:59.634
[ Dramatic music swells ]

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:00.868
[ Music stops ]

00:07:03.501 --> 00:07:05.567
Family!
Guys, that was the signal.

00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:07.067
We practiced this like 12 times.

00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:09.100
Thank you.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:12.434
Forgot all about my family,
didn't you, goddess?

00:07:12.434 --> 00:07:13.667
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.667 --> 00:07:15.567
-"It's all about family!"

00:07:15.567 --> 00:07:17.901
Zachary Levi!

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:22.234
"Shazam! Fury of the Gods" is in
theaters and IMAX this Friday.

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:23.767
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:25.634
Stick around. Go see it!
-Go see it, go see it!

